man.glb, woman.glb, boy.glb and girl.glb in this directory are adapted
works, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
licence (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Source: Human Reference Atlas 3D reference objects (HuBMAP CCF), the Visible
Human male and female, release v2.0, models/3d-vh-m-united.glb.zip and
models/3d-vh-f-united.glb.7z (https://github.com/hubmapconsortium/ccf-releases),
derived from the National Library of Medicine's Visible Human Project.
Licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://github.com/hubmapconsortium/ccf-3d-reference-object-library).

Changes: cut into one mesh per region and side as named in
src/body/regions.ts, plus one mesh each for the skin, the rest of the
skeleton and the thymus; other structures (eyes, vessels, nerves, lymph
node, reproductive organs, larynx, bronchi) left out; welded, simplified
with meshoptimizer, quantised and meshopt-compressed by tools/body/build.mjs.
boy.glb and girl.glb are the male and female interiors moved and resized,
organ by organ, to paediatric reference measurements
(components/body/references.json), inside an outline made from the
MakeHuman base mesh and macro targets (CC0 1.0,
makehumancommunity/makehuman at a8bc2d54); growth plates cut in the femur
and tibia. No warranty.

The code in this repository is MIT; this licence covers only the mesh.
